Ladybird leaves pending children hidden when computing styles below a
display:none ancestor. A retained SVG resource can require those styles
without revealing ordinary descendants.

Blink keeps hidden style resolution separate from attachment in
Element::RecalcOwnStyle. It treats an IsEnsuredInDisplayNone record as
absent before deciding if a style change requires reattachment.

WebKit stops ordinary descendant traversal at display:none in
Style::TreeResolver::resolveComposedTree, while allowing SVG containers
that still require renderers to resolve their descendants.

Gecko gates descendant traversal on the element being displayed in
recalc_style_at, and resolves hidden styles on demand through
resolve_style. Ladybird likewise keeps hidden style computation separate
from revealing descendants.
